                <div style="width:100%"> <!--  Start First Yellow Heading Text  -->
                    <h2 style="padding: 70px 0px 10px 0px; text-align:center;margin-left: -61px;display:none;">STEP-1: Entry
                        Test  <br/><span style="color:red;display:none;">For Entry Test procedures please <a
                                    href="https://admission.uet.edu.pk/Modules/EntryTest/Default.aspx">click here</a></span></h2>
                    <h3 style="text-align: center; color:red;display:none;">For Entry Test
                            Registration <a href="https://admission.uet.edu.pk/Modules/EntryTest/Default.aspx"> Please click here</a> [Last Date :
                            29<sup>th</sup> February, 2024]</h3>
                            <h3 style="text-align: center;color:red;display:none;">Entry test will be conducted from 11<sup>th</sup> to 15<sup>th</sup> March 2024 by UET Lahore. </h3>
                        <h3 style="text-align: center;color:red;display:none;">ECAT was conducted by UET Lahore from 03<sup>rd</sup> to 07<sup>th</sup> June 2024. </h3>
                        <h3 style="text-align: center;color:red;display:none">ECAT  will be conducted by UET Lahore from 13<sup>th</sup> to 17<sup>th</sup> March 2025. </h3>
                    <!-- <h2 style="padding: 30px 0px 10px 0px; text-align:center;display:none">STEP-2: Admission Procedure <br/><span style="color:red;">(Only those candidates are eligible to apply who appeared in ECAT-2025 (Phase-I & Phase-II)/Equivalent. Entry Test is not required for BS Physics and Mathematics.)<br/></span> -->
                       <h2 style="padding: 30px 0px 10px 0px; text-align:center;display:none"> Admission Procedure <br/><span style="color:red;">(Only those candidates are eligible to apply who appeared in TCAT/ECAT-2025 (Phase-I & Phase-II)/Equivalent. Entry Test is not required for BS Physics and Mathematics.)<br/></span>
                   <span style="display:none;">[Start Date: 10<sup>th</sup> June, 2024; End Date: 22<sup>nd</sup> August, 2022]</span>
                    </h2>
                   <h3 style="text-align: center; color:red;display:none;">(Admissions will be announced after ECAT-2024. Only those candidate will be able to apply who will appear in ECAT-2024, being conducted by UET Lahore.)</h3>
					<h3 style="padding: 20px 0px 10px 25px;text-decoration: underline;">Application Processing Fee <span style="color:red;display:none">[For <a href="Admission_Eligibility.php">Group 01</a> and <a href="Admission_Eligibility.php">Group 02</a> sepearate application processing fee is required]</span></h3>
                    
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%;">Application processing fee of Rs. 4000/- can be deposited through HBL digital banking against candidate's CNIC/Form-B number by following any of below mentioned modes:
                    <ol style="padding-left: 90px;width: 90%;line-height: 170%;">
                        <li>Non HBL Account Holders (Konnect App, Konnect Shops/Agents) selecting "UET Taxila Admission Processing"</li>
                        <li>HBL Account Holders (HBL Internet Banking, HBL Mobile App) selecting "UET Taxila Admission Processing"</li>                        
                    </ol>                    
                    </p>
					<div  style="font-weight: bold;text-align: center;color: red;margin-top: 10px;font-size: 15px;">
                        Without application fee your application will not be considered.
                    </div>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%;font-size: 15px;font-weight: bold;margin-top: 10px;">To view the detailed process of "how to submit application processing fee" <a href="ApplicationProcessingFee.php">Click Here</a></p>
                    
                    <h3 style="padding: 20px 0px 10px 25px;text-decoration: underline;">Instructions for Online Filling of Application Form
                        (F-I) <span style="color:red;">[For <span style="color:red;"><a href="Admission_Eligibility.php">Group 01</a> and <a href="Admission_Eligibility.php">Group 02</a> sepearate online application forms (F-I) are required]</span></h3>
                    <ol style="padding-left: 50px;width: 90%;line-height: 170%;">
                        <li style="display:none;">
                        Visit the nearest designated TCS Center <a href="ProspectusAvailability.php">(TCS Centers)</a> for submission of application processing fee Rs. 1500/- <strong>(Rs. 1450/- Application Processing Fee + Rs. 50/- TCS Charges)</strong> and obtain computerized deposit slip having <strong style="color:red;"> 15 digit </strong>  <strong style="color:red;"> Ref # </strong><span style="color:red;">[If 14 digit, make it 15 by adding 0 to the extreme left]</span>.
                            <ul style="padding: 5px 18px;">
                                <li>Please, provide your ECAT roll number as registration number to TCS Staff</li>
                                <li>Please, ask TCS Staff to deposit admission application processing fee for UET Taxila</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>                        
                        <li style="display:none;">
                            Submit Fee <strong>Rs. 1700/-</strong> (Prospectus Charges + Processing Fee + TCS chargers)
                            in TCS center and get receipt having consignment number (CN No.). 
                        </li>
                        <li style="display:none;">
                            Fee will be submitted in HBL UET Taxila <strong>Account Title: 'UET Taxila Recurring'
                                No. 19157900213501</strong> on deposit slip available in HBL UET, Taxila. In this case
                            the candidate will submit only <strong>Rs. 1450/- </strong>(Prospectus Charges + Processing
                            Fee paid at once). <strong style="color:red;">Ref # </strong>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Visit online admission portal <a href="http://admissions.uettaxila.edu.pk">admissions.uettaxila.edu.pk</a>
                            and click on MY UET button for registration with UET Taxila.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            For registration click registration button and provide the following information.
                            <ol style="list-style-type: lower-roman;padding-left: 30px;width: 90%;line-height: 170%;">
                                <li>CNIC/Form B number without dashes.</li>
                                <li>Set your password</li>
                                <li>TCAT/ECAT/Equivalent Roll No. <span style="color:red;">(Not Required for BS Mathematics and Physics)</span></li>
                                <li style="display:none;"><span>TCS <strong style="color:red;">Ref # (15 digit)</strong> <span style="color:red;">[If 14 digit, make it 15 by adding 0 to the extreme left]</span></li>
                                <li style="display:none;">Deposit date</li>
                                <li style="display:none;">Name of TCS Center</li>
                                <li style="display:none;">Upload the image of deposit slip</li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                        <li>Sign in now.</li>
                        <li>Fill the personnel information educational information, applicable options and preference
                            and submit it online.
                        </li>
                        <li>The applicant can sign in again and again in to see/edit his/her data until the submission
                            of application online.
                        </li>
                        <li>While filling the preference table, fill the column for preference very carefully. The order
                            of preference once given shall be final and cannot be changed subsequently of the submission
                            of application for online.
                        </li>
                        <li>Under the column Category choose only among “A” (open merit), “S” (Partially Subsidized) and “X” (children of overseas
                            Pakistani). The other categories will be adjusted
                            automatically depending upon his applicable option.
                        </li>
                        <li>As per schedule mentioned at <a href="http://admissions.uettaxila.edu.pk">admissions.uettaxila.edu.pk</a>
                            check merit lists.
                        </li>
                        <li>If the name of applicant appears in the merit list, he will visit his "My UET" account for further instructions.
                        </li>
                        <li>The applicant will upload all required documents as per the instructiuons at "My UET" account.
                        </li>
                        <li style="color: red; font-size: 15px; display:none;">The admission offer to “Not Eligible” candidates will
                            be cancelled whereas the “Eligible” candidates will be issued call letter and bank challan.
                        </li>
                        <li style="display:none;">After depositing fee in HBL, UET, Taxila branch the candidate will submit the following
                            documents in the Admission Office within the time period of a particular merit list:
                            <ol style="list-style-type: lower-roman;padding-left: 30px;width: 90%;line-height: 170%;">
                                <li>Bank Challan receipt in support of the University Dues deposited in the Habib Bank
                                    Ltd. University of Engineering and Technology Taxila Branch.
                                </li>
                                <li>Medical Certificate (F-V) duly signed and stamped by the District Medical
                                    Superintendent or the Medical Office of the University or a Commissioned Medical
                                    officer.
                                </li>
                                <li>Ten attested and most recent photographs.</li>
                                <li>Attested Certificate of parent’s /guardian’s income.</li>
                                <li>Original degrees, certificates and result card of SSC, HSSC, BSc, GCE(A), Diploma of
                                    Associate Engineers or the equivalent qualifications and their duplicate attested
                                    photocopies.
                                </li>
                                <li>Original Marks Sheet of Entry Test</li>
                                <li>Original NCC certificate (if applicable)</li>
                                <li>Original Domicile certificate</li>
                                <li>Attested copy of National CNIC/Form B</li>
                                <li>Bio-Data Sheet (F-VI) duly completed</li>
                                <li>Undertaking (F-VII) on a Stamp Paper of Rs. 50/- (Stamp Paper also attested by
                                    1<sup>st</sup> Class Magistrate/Oath Commissioner
                                </li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display:none;">
                            <strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Notification of
                                Selection</strong><br/>
                            A list of selectees will be displayed on official University web site.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Important consideration in
                                next merit lists:</strong> Admissions are granted on merit and according
                            to preferences given by the applicants. An
                            applicant who secures admission in a discipline
                            of his lower preference and he desires to be
                            considered in next merit lists, MUST pay the 1st semester dues of university and upload
                            all the required documents on "My UET" account. If he fails to do so, his name would
                            be excluded from any future merit lists and his
                            admission would be cancelled.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Freezing in any given Discipline and
                                Category</strong><br/>
                            If an applicant requests in writing to retain the discipline and category in which he has
                            been selected for admission
                            on merit, then he will not have any right to claim his admission in any other discipline and
                            category of higher or
                            lower merit if a seat falls vacant in any discipline. Applicant desiring to freeze
                            category/discipline should have to
                            apply in person on prescribed form for this purpose before the next merit list is displayed.
                        </li>
                        <li style="display:none;">
                            <strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Relaxation on Time
                                Limit</strong><br/>
                            If a selectee is prevented by unavoidable circumstances from timely fulfilment of the
                            requirements laid down in 29.1 and 29.2 (Admission 2024 Guidelines / Prospectus). he should intimate the
                            Convener Admission Committee
                            about it within prescribed time limit along with relevant documentary proof. The Convener
                            Admission Committee may at his discretion, grant relaxation in the time limit, which shall not
                            exceed Three Days.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Forfeiture of Right for
                                Admission</strong><br/>
                            A selectee who fails to fulfill the requirements laid down in 29.1 and 29.2 (Admission 2024 Guidelines / Prospectus) within the
                            prescribed time limit shall forfeit his right
                            of admission and will not be considered in
                            subsequent merit lists.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong style="text-decoration: underline;color: red;">Provisional Admission</strong><br/>
                            On fulfillment of the obligations mentioned in 29.1 and 29.2 (Admission 2024 Guidelines / Prospectus) a selectee
                            will be admitted to
                            the university. This admission shall, however, be provisional un till all the original
                            degrees or certificates, submitted by him, have been verified for their veracity.
                        </li>


                    </ol>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">
                        i. On the web-link click on My UET button. Enter your CNIC/B Form No. issued by NADRA and set
                        password then click Register
                        button for registration with UET to access the application Form. </br>
                    </p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">ii. Candidate can now
                        Sign in. </p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">iii. Please fill the
                        personal information, applicable options, Educational information and preferences. </br>
                    </p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">iv. The candidate can
                        Sign in again and again to see/edit his/her data until he /she submits his/her final printed
                        application
                        Form <strong>BY HAND/BY POST</strong> in Admission Office, UET, Taxila. </br>
                    </p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;"> v. After filling the
                        Application Form online according to given instructions, applicant will get its printout, sign
                        it and
                        attach requisite documents, along with the Declaration Form (F-0) (available in the Prospectus)
                        and then submit <strong>BY HAND/BY POST</strong> in
                        the Admission Office, UET, Taxila. </p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">vi. Only one application
                        form is to be submitted for any number of disciplines and
                        categories you apply for both <b>Campuses (Taxila & Chakwal)</b>. Fill the column for
                        preferences very carefully. </br>
                        vii. The Order of preferences once given shall be final and cannot be
                        changed subsequently, after the submission of Application Form in Admission Office. </br>
                    </p>
                    <p style="text-align: center; display: none;"><img style="width: 700px;height: 300px;"
                                                                       src="images/Advertise_urdu.png"/></p>
                    <h3 style="padding: 20px 0px 10px 25px; display: none;"> Notification of Selection</h3>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">
                        A list of selectees will be displayed on official University web site. </br></p>

                    <h3 style="padding: 20px 0px 10px 25px; color:#ff0000; display: none;"> Important: Consideration in
                        next merit lists</h3>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%;display: none;">
                        Admissions are granted on merit and according to preferences given by the applicants. An
                        applicant who secures
                        admission in a discipline of his lower preference and he desires to be considered in next merit
                        lists. MUST submit
                        all the UNIVERSITY dues and ORIGINAL documents. If he fails to do so, his name would be excluded
                        from any future
                        merit lists and his admission would be cancelled. </br></p>
                    <h3 style="padding: 20px 0px 10px 25px; display: none;">
                        Freezing in any given Discipline and Category</h3>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%; display: none;">
                        If an applicant requests in writing to retain the discipline and category in which he has been
                        selected for admission
                        on merit, then he will not have any right to claim his admission in any other discipline and
                        category of higher or
                        lower merit if a seat falls vacant in any discipline. Applicant desiring to freeze
                        category/discipline should have to
                        apply in person on prescribed form for this purpose before the next merit list is
                        displayed.</br></p>
                    <p style="padding-left: 50px; width:90%; line-height: 170%;">&nbsp;</p>
